# Windows batch files must always keep CRLF line endings, regardless of
# whoever commits or checks them out (cmd.exe's parser is unreliable with
# LF-only line endings). This overrides any local core.autocrlf setting,
# so a plain "git clone" or GitHub's "Download ZIP" always produces a
# working .bat file.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
